The test constructs a line contour with `ax.contour(...)`, then reads `contour_set._contour_generator` and calls `create_contour(test_level)`. In `lib/matplotlib/contour.py`, `QuadContourSet._process_args` creates that generator via `contourpy.contour_generator(..., line_type=contourpy.LineType.SeparateCode, ...)`, so `create_contour(level)` returns parallel lists of vertex arrays and code arrays, one pair per contour segment. For the selected middle level `levels[4]`, that call yields 3 segment arrays and 3 matching code arrays, and the first segment’s vertex array is a 2D coordinate array with shape `(47, 2)`.

## Answer
{"codes_count":3,"first_vertex_shape":[47,2],"vertices_count":3}
